From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 04:25:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Add a switch to show the init objects
 in debugfs

The firmware's init objects (Main, Globals, Runtime, the power and
performance object, the activity objects and the rest of the 31) are
built by the host before the firmware starts, and the firmware then
updates some of them. To compare them byte for byte with what macOS
hands the same firmware, both versions are needed, and nothing exposes
either today.

Add the load-time parameter g16_init_dump. When it is set, the driver
keeps the encoder's private images of the 31 objects and creates the
read-only debugfs file aurora-g16/initdata. It prints each object's id,
name, GPU address and size, then every non-zero 32-byte row of the
encoded image and of the live bytes. The log entry and data objects
print their header line only. The default, 0, keeps nothing and creates
no file.

Assisted-by: LLM
